period?). But several warnings for a single post seems a bit like a
luckless motorist who gets stopped by a traffic cop, and is charged with
'speeding', 'driving without due care and attention' and one or two others.

If several violations of List Rules occured in a single post, or maybe also
including subsequent posts that were sent before the warning would have been
received, how about issuing a warning for each violation, but the warnings
would each run concurrently instead of consecutively? So they would only
count as one warning under the 'totting up procedure'. Allowing three days'
grace before any further consecutive warning(s) could be issued, this would
mean that a real List Criminal could be exiled after 9 days. (And really
serious crimes like those of Pandit could be dealt with by immediate
expulsion in any case - giving 3 warnings for deliberately slagging off Exi, 
infringing copyrights etc would be too lenient). Sorry, Harry!

Of course, after all warnings had been used up, each individual case would
be treated on its merits -- some people would get a relatively short period
of suspension and others would be permanently banned, depending on the
gravity of their crimes.

Another point: if someone had received two or three warnings, could they
be given the opportunity to 'earn' the repeal of a warning by writing
polite, constructive, thoughtful posts? This would provide an incentive to
a character to reform and produce quality postings -- each time they wrote
a good post they could have one warning annulled at the discretion of the
List Management. (Although if they started flaming immediately afterwards
someone would be on them like a ton of bricks!)

